        <briefdescription>
<para>Reads indexes and applies snapshot deletion vectors in the selected partition/bucket. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Supports fixed-bucket append tables without real-time mode or data evolution. If any input has indexes, all source row counts and the output row count must fit int32. <simplesect kind="note"><para>IMPORTANT: Returned index metadata uses each file&apos;s schema. Callers must handle schema changes.</para>
</simplesect>
Uses the same file name and physical row order as <ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_append_file_compaction_1ab216df5f7e54bd24a060fb4c7618585a" kindref="member">AppendFileCompaction::Execute</ref>. Callers must retain source files and use the same snapshot deletion state for execution.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>table_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_table" kindref="compound">Table</ref> root path. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>branch</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Branch name; empty selects main. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>partition</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Complete partition values; empty for an unpartitioned table. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bucket</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bucket containing the input files. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>file_names</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Nonempty set of unambiguous live file basenames. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>snapshot_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Snapshot to scan; nullopt fixes the latest snapshot once per call. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>options</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Overrides for the latest schema options. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>file_system</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>File system; nullptr selects one from options. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pool</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Memory pool; nullptr uses the default. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>executor</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Manifest scan executor; nullptr uses the default. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Index metadata and row mappings, or an error. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
